A steel ball of diameter $0.080\text{ m}$ is released from rest and falls vertically in air, as illustrated in Fig. 2.1.

{{figure:figure_2_1}}

A horizontal beam of light of negligible width is a vertical distance of $0.280\text{ m}$ below the bottom of the ball when it is released. The ball falls through and breaks the beam of light.

